      "content": "Your observation that evolution might favor certain traits is ecologically valid, but science has not identified a natural human phenotype capable of 3–4 hour sleep needs or processing speeds beyond normal waking peak performance. While \"cryptic genius\" or high intelligence exists, neither guarantees extreme sleep efficiency nor instantaneous comprehension of complex material for all individuals. The feeling of hyper-sharpness can even be a desirable side effect of rationalizing your own biological imperatives, yet clinical data suggests such states are not evidence of a new species but rather intense stress masking itself as a productivity breakthrough.",
